      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "text": "\ninference      ( inferences    plural  )\n1)  An inference is a conclusion that you draw about something by\n    using information that you already have about it.   (=conclusion)  \n\n2)  Inference is the act of drawing conclusions about something on\n    the basis of information that you already have.  ",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\ninference      ( inferences    plural  )\n1)  An inference is a conclusion that you draw about something by\n    using information that you already have about it.   (=conclusion)  \n\n2)  Inference is the act of drawing conclusions about something on\n    the basis of information that you already have.  ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
